--TEST--
An object's string property replaced inside a `try` by an interpolation of itself has its new value in the `finally` — `rule:types/a-replaced-value-is-changed-in-place`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Box {
    public string $text = "ab";
}

Box $box = new Box();
try {
    // The new string is the property followed by `x`, so the property is `abx`.
    $box->text = "{$box->text}x";
} finally {
    echo "finally: ", $box->text, "\n";
}
echo $box->text, "\n";
--EXPECT--
finally: abx
abx
